# Content block schema

Blocks are returned in `get_contents_from_docx` → `items` and passed to `write_contents_to_docx` → `contents`.

Discriminator: `block_type` — `"paragraph"` or `"table"`.

## ParagraphBlock

```json
{
  "block_type": "paragraph",
  "runs": [
    {
      "text": "Hello world",
      "bold": null,
      "italic": null,
      "font_name": null,
      "font_size_pt": null
    }
  ],
  "style": {
    "name": "Normal",
    "style_type": "paragraph"
  }
}
```

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `block_type` | `"paragraph"` | yes | Discriminator |
| `runs` | `RunFormat[]` | yes | Text segments; may be empty |
| `style` | `StyleHint \| null` | no | Style **name reference** only |

### RunFormat

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `text` | `string` | Run text (may be empty string) |
| `bold` | `bool \| null` | `null` = inherit from paragraph style |
| `italic` | `bool \| null` | |
| `font_name` | `string \| null` | e.g. `"Courier New"` |
| `font_size_pt` | `number \| null` | Points |

Concatenate all `runs[].text` for full paragraph text.

### StyleHint

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `name` | `string` | Paragraph style name in the document |
| `style_type` | `string` | Default `"paragraph"` |

**Not** a full style definition. Fetch definitions via `get_styles_from_docx`.

## TableBlock

```json
{
  "block_type": "table",
  "rows": [
    [
      {
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "block_type": "paragraph",
            "runs": [{ "text": "Cell text", "bold": null, "italic": null, "font_name": null, "font_size_pt": null }],
            "style": { "name": "Normal", "style_type": "paragraph" }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  ]
}
```

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `block_type` | `"table"` | Discriminator |
| `rows` | `TableCellBlock[][]` | Row-major; each cell has nested paragraphs |

### TableCellBlock

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `paragraphs` | `ParagraphBlock[]` | One or more paragraphs per cell |

Cells do not have their own style — styling is on nested paragraphs.

## Paginated read envelope

`get_contents_from_docx` wraps blocks:

```json
{
  "items": [ "...blocks..." ],
  "total": 48,
  "offset": 0,
  "limit": 10,
  "has_more": true,
  "source_path": "/absolute/path/file.docx"
}
```

| Field | Notes |
|---|---|
| `total` | Total block count in document body |
| `has_more` | `true` when `offset + limit < total` |
| `source_path` | Resolved absolute path |

## Write response

`write_contents_to_docx`:

```json
{
  "file_path": "/absolute/path/output.docx",
  "blocks_written": 48,
  "created": true
}
```

`created: true` when the file did not exist before the call.

## Rules for agents

1. Preserve `block_type` when round-tripping content.
2. Keep `style.name` references — do not replace with inline formatting unless intentional.
3. Table structure: preserve row/column count and nested paragraph order.
4. Omitted optional fields may be treated as `null` on read; include required fields on write.
